    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$\\overline{A\\cap B}=\\overline A\\cap\\overline B$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "False.",
      "worked": "False. Let $U=\\{1,2\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{A\\cap B}&=\\overline{\\varnothing},\\\\\\overline{A\\cap B}&=\\{1,2\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cap\\overline B&=\\{2\\}\\cap\\{1\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cap\\overline B&=\\varnothing.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sets differ.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
